  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "The feminine-consort modes of the North Indian ragamala system, systematised in the medieval raga-ragini classifications and painted in the Rajput and Pahari ragamala albums from the sixteenth century, and surviving in performance through gharana khayal and dhrupad treatments of Todi, Asavari, Bhairavi, Gauri and Malkauns's consorts — slow unmetered alap over tanpura drone, then a bandish in vilambit and drut laya on tabla, with sarangi or sitar shadowing a heavily meend- and gamak-inflected vocal line.",
